not only are mentors in battle shown in  anime called but they also tend to be  memorable besides the main characters  and villains these people tend to be the  best or most prominent side characters  and they serve to guide the hero on his  quest to become stronger anyway you can  say they're the real mvp unfortunately  being an anime mentor also comes with  the well-known occupational hazard but  we're not here to see mentors dying are  we we have a separate list for sad  moments and all but for today we're here  to bask in their glory to see them at  their peak at their best and what better  way to show it in a battle shonen than  to give focus to some of the best and  most memorable battles featuring them so  strap yourselves in as we take a ride  through some of my favorite mental  battles in action shonen we start things  off with benimaru vs holy soul  benimaru and cool fights it seems to go  together we already featured this  awesome mentor before so how about  another fight this time against holy  souls shadows anyone out for a one man  army fight because benimaru brings the  heat when he single-handedly takes down  the holy soul shadows in spectacular  fashion even when they try to mob him he  simply uses them as a showcase of power  blasting them multiple times over even  when the shadows look like they landed a  hit it just became a scene to build up  benimaru's spectacular finish one of the  nice fire force fights for us to  remember although calling it a fight  would be a bit of a stretch domination  is more like it  [Music]  is  up next is koro sensei versus yanagisava  jigokuno yonayo  i've talked long about goro sensei being  one of the most overpowered characters  in anime but i haven't featured an  assassination classroom fight at all  have i well that's gonna change today  and we end that with a banger of a fight  a climactic showdown between goro sensei  and yanagisava is pretty much all you  want from a final fight in a series like  assassination classroom yanagisama  played the final boss role to perfection  and gave goro sensei a run for his money  the fight's filled with revelations  intense attacks and jaw-dropping  sequences it also has its share of drama  featuring guyana and even reaper 2.0  upon his defeat truly an impressive and  awesome way to wrap up this anime that's  given his fans some of their best years  [Applause]  we take to the fate universe for the  next entry chiron vs  achilles chiron versus achilles is one  of the more underlooked fights and i  don't blame you fate apocrypha is in my  eyes the most niche anime of the fate  universe it doesn't have the legacy of  stay night or zero nor does it have such  a huge game and cinematic presence as  grand order yeah it keeps up the fake  tradition of having crisp eye-catching  fights and this kiron vs achilles fight  is the poster child for that i talked  about this fight in one of my best  hand-to-hand fight videos because it's  just that good it's a good old broad  where the anime team really went out of  their way to capture the action and the  barrage of attacks the two throw at each  other if you're looking for amazingly  animated fights in fantasy action anime  then feel free to give this one a shot  all for one versus all might is the  definition of hype  [Music]  one thing my hero academia does so well  is build hype he spent a lot of time  building all might as this unstoppable  force of good someone even the strongest  villains tremble at the site of he  easily wins all his fights and saves his  students numerous times in impressive  fashion but every light has a shadow an  apt foil that serves to provide a  balance in power and that's why everyone  was so excited to hear that all might  was finally going to fight his  counterpart all for one and the fight  delivered there's just this magical  feeling seeing the two strongest forces  in my hero academia duke it out for real  all for one versus all might is a fight  that left everyone both in universe and  out of universe in awe the united states  of smash moment here is still one of my  favorite moments even as more seasons  have come and gone another good thing to  know is that this is one status altering  fight for the whole universe glad to see  all might retiring in style and if  seeing all might's greatest moments got  you all hyped imagine how hyped i was  when the channel hit a million subs i'm  here to just take a moment to thank you  for all the help in getting the channel  to reach that landmark it really means  everything to me thank you but let's not  stop there okay heck if my newer videos  continue to give you fun times then why  don't you hit that like button subscribe  and share the channel with your shown  and loving friends we've got loads of  videos here and i'd be more than happy  to see the vinichu family grow hope you  have a good time ahead with the rest of  the list nothing's a better definition  of constant improvement than black  clover and this fighting body zip  [Music]  dante one of the best fights black clove  has given us and it's fitting that it  happens towards the end of the anime  saving the best for last yeah am i right  what i like about this fight isn't just  the actual fighting yet the fighting's  great and i'm all for seeing more of  yami's dark magic it's all shades of  awesome but what i feel is the most  important element of this fight is how  it proves arsdas development you'd be  hard-pressed to find that little  annoying kid from early to be this  badass and here he stands toe-to-toe  fighting alongside his captain against  one of the most powerful enemies they've  encountered so far aston matured and  badass at this point and you bet it's a  source of pride for yami his pupils all  grown up has become one of the most  reliable allies he can ever ask for  here's another amazing final fight with  gintoki versus futsuro  what better way for gintama the final to  end with the grandest battle of them all  kintoki finally faces utsuru in a  spectacle that gintama fans will forever  remember one underrated thing about this  fight is the foreshadowing remember when  this was teased all the way back with  everyone thinking takasugi is going to  be the final villain just an added layer  of bonus to what ends up being a really  amazing fight gintama is no stranger to  making the fans feel a rollercoaster of  emotions that this fight encapsulates  that in a big way i also love how the  fight turns out to be quite methodical  instead of showering us with fireworks  there's the whole use of silence and  flashbacks to build everything up as the  two go at it it truly adds to the moment  the solemn ambiance and it gives each  blow more gravity if you get what i'm  saying a great battle that serves as a  great finale one that amazes us while  reminding us of the journey to get here  go joe versus jogo is next on the list  this one's a favorite not specifically  because of some mind-blowing fight  choreography but simply because of how  much of a landmark moment it was it's  the first time we see gojo flex his  power over someone and mapa just had to  put up some of their best work in the  art department for this let's be real  this early in the show it's never going  to be some intense back and forth  between the mentor character showing off  his strength and a character who didn't  seem like such a big threat it's just  gojo showing how superior he is by using  this as a tutorial level to his pupil  but boy did he make a pretty show out of  it i'm not sure if i'd rank this above  hollow purple if we're talking about  spectacular gojo moments but it's the  one that gained more buzz from the  community and that's understandable  because the latter's the icing on top of  the already amazing hanami fight  here's another supernatural anime fight  on the list tengen vs gutaro  [Music]  it's kind of tough to lock this fight  down with a start point to an end point  the climactic battle in demon slayer's  entertainment district asks pretty much  a chain of fights with participants  tagging in and out of action and being  given their respective focus that's also  what makes its presentation so  interesting and unique the whole  sequence has its fair share of epic  moments but i think that the tangent  parts are my favorite the nezuko parts  are cool and all but it's when tengen  takes the forefront do i feel the most  excited every time we see a pillar in  action it's always cool but tengen takes  it a step further with his blitzing  style combining speed with power and  taking the fight to the upper moon duo  dangerous joining the fight gives the  battle a much welcome boost in height  being the first time our protagonist  joins his mentor in a fight to this  level  finally we have kakashi vs obito  kakashi versus obito for the most part  seems to be a fight that gets hype based  on the history it's a long time coming  between the two and we know it's gonna  be big when we see the longtime friends  turned enemies finally face off with one  another it's that naruto versus sasuke  of another generation and the anime made  sure to hammer that point home i mean in  some ways this one's even better than  the actual naruto versus sasuke fight  it's a battle that's all about blazing  speed combined with trademark naruto  magic system i also like how physical  combat comes into play as the two blitz  each other there are some rather funny  comments that claim that this is the  most actual ninja-like fight in the  series but hey can we disagree with that  just look at these two go it's a fight  that has a good story great gravity and  huge stakes all done in a package though  while doesn't match the special effects  extravaganza modern fights have still  gave us a good moment to remember  and that wraps up today's list mentor  fights are the coolest aren't they i  hope you enjoyed the video once again  thank you for watching i hope to see you  again in the next video which is  scheduled to come out in just a few days  time make sure to bring your friends  along for the ride too
 

